WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.118
Alana Yzola: Tierra
Whack is quickly becoming

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:08.090
one of the brightest new stars in hip-hop.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.390
She's gotten cosigns from hip-hop
juggernauts like Meek Mill

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.060
and appeared on Beyoncé's
"The Gift" album.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.950
But what really makes
Tierra Whack one of a kind

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.560
is her video style.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.290
The MC dropped her visual
album, "Whack World,"

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.370
with undeniable success.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.960
With that album, she released 15

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.900
wildly creative music videos.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.675
Tierra Whack: The most fun
video to shoot was definitely...

00:00:31.675 --> 00:00:35.233
...

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:39.370
so many, 15, ah....

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.830
Yzola: Each video comes
with a host of references

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.321
and eye-popping visuals

00:00:43.321 --> 00:00:45.537
that match her fresh take on hip-hop.

00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:48.850
In addition to her lyricism
and rapid-fire flow,

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.080
here's why her groundbreaking video style

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.143
is making her an artist to watch.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.500
Tierra Whack first appeared
on the scene at age 15

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.575
when she did an impromptu freestyle

00:01:00.575 --> 00:01:03.060
for one of Philly's
underground rap collectives.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.410
Whack: When I started
freestyling in Philly,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.393
I was really young,

00:01:05.393 --> 00:01:06.770
and that was just, like, something to do;

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:07.880
everybody was doing it.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.015
And it kinda, like,
helped me to get my buzz,

00:01:10.015 --> 00:01:11.520
you know, in the streets and everything.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:14.140
Yzola: The video of her
rapping got posted online

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.420
and racked up tens of
thousands of views overnight.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.240
From there, she started
showcasing her talents

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.180
on local radio stations,

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.386
freestyling for the likes
of Meek Mill and A$AP Rocky,

00:01:25.386 --> 00:01:27.600
who compared her flow to Kendrick Lamar's.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.285
Whack: Eventually, I
was like, you know what?

00:01:29.285 --> 00:01:31.010
I think I really wanna take
this rap stuff serious.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.340
So, I started getting into the studio,

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.580
just really trying to, like, write hooks.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.685
Yzola: She recorded her first
hit single, "Mumbo Jumbo,"

00:01:39.685 --> 00:01:43.920
in 2017 the day after
getting her teeth pulled.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.040
Because of her loopy state at the time,

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.507
the lyrics sound like total gibberish.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:49.340
♪ All d--- night ♪

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.173
♪ Been awake ♪

00:01:50.173 --> 00:01:51.054
♪ Aw yeah ♪

00:01:51.054 --> 00:01:52.130
♪ No ♪

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.188
Yzola: In other words, it's an extreme

00:01:54.188 --> 00:01:56.480
and catchy take on mumble rap.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.440
But it was "Mumbo Jumbo's"
dentist-office-themed video

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.430
that really made the song go viral,

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.323
turning Solange into a fan.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.680
She also earned praise
from Kevin Abstract.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.590
Abstract called "Mumbo
Jumbo" the best music video

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:12.930
he'd seen all year.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.453
But "Mumbo Jumbo" was only the beginning.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.900
Tierra took her video
game to a whole new level

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.160
with her debut album, "Whack World."

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.570
The project contains 15 tracks,

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.740
each clocking in at 60 seconds

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.360
and accompanied by its own video.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.380
Each one of the video's concepts
is distinct from the next.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.800
Yet, the whole thing flows
from beginning to end

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.765
like a short film,
seamlessly taking us through

00:02:39.765 --> 00:02:41.520
the weird and captivating world

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.030
of Tierra Whack's mind.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.170
To bring her vision to life,
Tierra enlisted the help

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.430
of Thibaut Duverneix and his team

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.860
at Gentilhomme studio in Montreal.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.401
Thibaut Duverneix: If I could categorize

00:02:52.401 --> 00:02:53.767
the style of "Whack World,"

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:56.300
I would say it's made for people

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.591
who have a very short attention span,

00:02:58.591 --> 00:02:59.783
and it's like a candy.

00:02:59.783 --> 00:03:02.441
Yzola: The project was
first released on Instagram,

00:03:02.441 --> 00:03:04.430
and it made clever use of the platform's

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.520
three-column grid design.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.890
Whack: I wrote all the
songs in 60 seconds.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.075
We made the beat, and I
was writing to the beat

00:03:11.075 --> 00:03:12.558
while the beat was getting made.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.720
We had the idea, like, solidified.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.430
Yzola: But shooting 15 one-minute videos,

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.982
each with its own set,
concept, and special effects,

00:03:20.982 --> 00:03:24.232
all in two days was no small undertaking.

00:03:24.232 --> 00:03:25.862
Duverneix: We thought
it was a great idea but

00:03:25.862 --> 00:03:28.100
also an amazing challenge.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.040
It meant, like, literally
creating 15 little films

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.470
that would eventually live
together on the platform.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.080
But we also wanted to make
it, like, a 15-minute,

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.570
standalone movie that we
could release on the internet.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.420
Yzola: One reason why Whack's projects

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.980
feel more like mini
films than music videos

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.640
is because they take inspiration

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.090
from her favorite movie genre: horror.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.470
Tierra had already showed
off her appreciation

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:53.420
for dark humor in early
videos, like "Mumbo Jumbo."

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.750
And Duverneix helped her
incorporate those themes

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.990
into "Whack World."

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:58.980
Like in her video for "Bugs Life,"

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.233
when Tierra pulls back her hoodie

00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:02.880
to reveal a grotesque, half-swollen face.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.080
Whack: I do not like summertime because

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:06.088
that's when the bugs come out,

00:04:06.088 --> 00:04:07.355
and I'm allergic to bug bites.

00:04:07.355 --> 00:04:09.334
Duverneix: So I was like,
let's make your face swollen

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:12.046
like you had, like, a
crazy allergic reaction.

00:04:12.046 --> 00:04:14.418
Whack: All my life I had to fight.

00:04:14.418 --> 00:04:15.800
What did you do to my face?

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:16.983
But then, also, "A Bug's Life"

00:04:16.983 --> 00:04:18.091
is one of my favorite movies.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.680
Like, so classic. Like, favorite ever.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.050
Yzola: Horror motifs is
something you'll see a lot of

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.170
in the visuals for "Whack World."

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:28.060
The surprisingly upbeat
song "Pet Cemetery"

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.960
references both the
terrifying Stephen King novel

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.412
and the kids' animated film
"All Dogs Go to Heaven."

00:04:34.412 --> 00:04:36.070
♪ All dogs go to heaven ♪

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.378
♪ Heaven ♪

00:04:37.378 --> 00:04:39.240
Yzola: The tombstone is also a nod

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.260
to the comedy-horror series "Being Human."

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.430
Sally Malik is a ghost on the show

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.020
whose character also died in 2010.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.290
The video captures the play
between light and dark,

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.925
showing Tierra hanging out with

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.358
giant, Muppet-like
creatures in a graveyard

00:04:55.358 --> 00:04:57.758
while singing about death and mourning.

00:04:57.758 --> 00:05:00.960
There's a lot of childhood
nostalgia in "Whack World."

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.550
"Dr. Seuss" draws inspiration
from "Alice in Wonderland."

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.810
"Fruit Salad" is based on
the song by The Wiggles.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.320
And the video concept for "Hungry Hippo"

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.640
is an irreverent play on the
classic Hasbro kids' game

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.520
Hungry Hungry Hippos, right
down to the color coding.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.236
Whack: The most fun video
to shoot was definitely...

00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:23.853
...

00:05:23.853 --> 00:05:28.743
so many, 15, ah...

00:05:28.743 --> 00:05:30.326
"Fruit Salad."

00:05:30.326 --> 00:05:31.511
♪ I did, I did ♪

00:05:31.511 --> 00:05:34.070
♪ I eat all my vegetables ♪

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:34.903
Yeah.

00:05:34.903 --> 00:05:37.810
Yzola: In the final video
for "Whack World," "Waze,"

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:41.380
Tierra sits in a room as it
fills up with soapy suds.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:44.470
Whack: Out of all my music
videos, the most challenging

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:45.830
was definitely "Waze."

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.140
"Waze" was crazy.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:51.930
I had to, like, sit in the
same, like, stance for, like,

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.810
it was so long, and I couldn't breathe.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.820
The bubbles smelled like bleach.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.495
Duverneix: She had to hold still,

00:05:57.495 --> 00:06:00.103
not coughing and, like, not crying.

00:06:00.103 --> 00:06:01.716
Also, what's funny is, like,

00:06:01.716 --> 00:06:04.331
in the track, you can hear her coughing.

00:06:04.331 --> 00:06:06.270
(coughing)
♪ One, two, three ♪

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.490
Duverneix: But she couldn't cough on set.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.610
Yzola: Tierra's vision
puts her next in line

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.710
in a series of true hip-hop originals.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.980
She cites the original
music-video queen, Missy Elliot,

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.480
amongst her biggest artistic influences,

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.457
along with other hip-hop vanguards,

00:06:21.457 --> 00:06:23.500
like Busta Rhymes and Kanye West.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:26.280
She also named OutKast
her favorite rap duo

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:30.500
and has referred to André
3000 as her "father."

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.649
From inspiration to execution,

00:06:32.649 --> 00:06:34.956
Whack has earned some serious accolades,

00:06:34.956 --> 00:06:36.850
especially after "Whack World."

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.640
She got a best music
video nod at the Grammys

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.593
for her visuals to "Mumbo Jumbo."

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.800
And now she's fresh off
landing a coveted spot

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.710
in the XXL Freshman Class.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:51.180
Pitchfork put "Whack World" at No. 9

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.990
on their list of the
50 best albums of 2018,

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.740
and Billboard put it on
their critic's picks list

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.070
of the 100 greatest music
videos in the 21st century.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.245
All right. So, guys, what did
you think of "Whack World?"

00:07:04.245 --> 00:07:06.970
And which tracks would you
like to see some visuals for?

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.670
Let us know in the comments below.

